{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And the sense of</b> וענשו אותו מאה כסף ('and they shall fine him a hundred silver'). The Master, of blessed memory, wrote in the Book of the Guide that since the marriage payment of the woman mentioned in the Torah is fifty silver, and this man who brings forth an evil name sought to cause her to lose her ketubah and to send her away with nothing, therefore the Torah imposed upon him to pay double, in the manner of (Exodus 22): ״אשר ירשיעון אלהים ישלם שנים לרעהו״, and in the manner of what we find concerning conspiring witnesses, who are punished according to their intent — so too this one who brings forth an evil name: he sought to come upon her by way of prostitution, therefore ויסרו אותו ('and they shall discipline him'); he sought to cause her to lose fifty, therefore וענשו אותו מאה ('and they shall fine him a hundred'); he sought to betray her and send her away, therefore לא יוכל לשלחה ('he shall not be able to send her away')."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Citation שמות כב left as chapter-only, as written; the quoted phrase is from Exodus 22:8."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:25.334235671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}